# threads: daily auto-wrapup backstop (docs/auto-wrapup.md) — runs after
# scan && weave, which refresh the activity data it reads. Deterministic and
# offline (zero model calls): it classifies every stale thread into terminal /
# blocked / A1 (abandoned, mechanically recoverable) / A2 (abandoned with a
# dirty worktree — never auto-touched) / B (parked and forgotten), writes
# ~/.threads/sweep/<date>.md, and sends one info flare on non-idle days.
# Report mode: dispatching wrap-up workers is config-gated ([sweep] mode in
# ~/.threads/config.toml) and stays OFF until Daniel flips it. Sources ~/.env
# and uses the PATH above for `gh` (PR state) and `git`.
#PAUSED# 49 7 * * * set -a; . /mnt/nw/home/d.tan/.env; set +a; /mnt/nw/home/d.tan/jarvis-monorepo/.venv/bin/threads sweep >> /mnt/nw/home/d.tan/.claude/logs/threads.log 2>&1

